# Optional Harness / Harness UI development and debugging environment template.
# Purpose-specific dev profiles live in dev/harness/.env.example and
# dev/harness-ui/.env.example; make cli loads dev/harness-ui/.env explicitly.
#
# Export only the settings needed by the Host, or explicitly launch it with:
# uv run --env-file .env a13n-harness-ui --no-update-check
# Do not overwrite an existing private .env when using this template.
# Nothing in the repository loads the root .env implicitly: Service development
# reads var/dev/service.toml (or SERVICE_CONFIG), Service E2E tests read the process
# environment, and make langfuse-* needs no configuration.
# Harness and Pydantic AI themselves read only the process environment.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Models
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Provider credentials are optional. Package installation never selects or
# enables a Provider.
#
# Direct model APIs:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# CO_API_KEY=
# CO_BASE_URL=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# HF_TOKEN=
#
# Google Vertex AI. GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS points to a local service
# account JSON file; Application Default Credentials may be used instead.
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=us-central1
#
# AWS Bedrock and Bedrock Mantle use the standard AWS credential chain. A local
# profile is preferable to copying long-lived access keys into `.env`.
# AWS_PROFILE=
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=
# AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=
#
# Azure OpenAI:
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_VERSION=
#
# Pydantic AI Gateway:
# PYDANTIC_AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
# PYDANTIC_AI_GATEWAY_BASE_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Harness Features
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local Envd development override. `make local-envd-test` loads the root `.env`
# only inside the target shell and otherwise uses target/debug/a13n-envd.
# A13N_ENVD_EXECUTABLE=target/debug/a13n-envd

# Media-understanding fallback. Configure each media kind that should be
# analyzed by a dedicated Pydantic AI Agent when the active AgentSpec
# model_config does not declare the corresponding native media capability.
# A13N_HARNESS_IMAGE_UNDERSTANDING_MODEL=google:gemini-3.7-flash
# A13N_HARNESS_VIDEO_UNDERSTANDING_MODEL=google:gemini-3.7-flash
# A13N_HARNESS_AUDIO_UNDERSTANDING_MODEL=google:gemini-3.7-flash
# Optional JSON objects are merged over the default {"temperature": 0.1}.
# A13N_HARNESS_IMAGE_UNDERSTANDING_MODEL_SETTINGS={"temperature":0.1}
# A13N_HARNESS_VIDEO_UNDERSTANDING_MODEL_SETTINGS={"temperature":0.1}
# A13N_HARNESS_AUDIO_UNDERSTANDING_MODEL_SETTINGS={"temperature":0.1}

# Web selection defaults. Provider objects and credentials remain Host run
# bindings; these values select only modes and named backend IDs. Setting one
# exact backend ignores its corresponding comma-separated priority.
# A13N_HARNESS_WEB_SEARCH_MODE=auto
# A13N_HARNESS_WEB_SEARCH_BACKEND=
# A13N_HARNESS_WEB_SEARCH_BACKEND_PRIORITY=brave,tavily
# A13N_HARNESS_WEB_SEARCH_CONTEXT_SIZE=medium
# A13N_HARNESS_WEB_SCRAPE_MODE=host
# A13N_HARNESS_WEB_SCRAPE_BACKEND=
# A13N_HARNESS_WEB_SCRAPE_BACKEND_PRIORITY=firecrawl,local

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Observation
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Observation is disabled by default. Enable signals only after configuring a
# matching OpenTelemetry provider/exporter profile.
A13N_HARNESS_TRACE_LEVEL=off
A13N_HARNESS_TRACE_CONTENT=none
A13N_HARNESS_METRICS=off
OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=agent-foundation-dev
OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=none
OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=none
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=http/protobuf

# Generic OTLP collector profile supporting traces and metrics:
# A13N_HARNESS_TRACE_LEVEL=verbose
# A13N_HARNESS_METRICS=standard
# OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=otlp
# OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:4318

# Logfire profile. Install the Logfire SDK and call logfire.configure() once at
# executable Host startup. A Host can make startup conditional on LOGFIRE_TOKEN.
# LOGFIRE_TOKEN=
# LOGFIRE_SERVICE_NAME=agent-foundation-dev
# LOGFIRE_SEND_TO_LOGFIRE=if-token-present
# A13N_HARNESS_TRACE_LEVEL=verbose
# A13N_HARNESS_METRICS=standard

# Local Langfuse trace profile. Apply these overrides after `make langfuse-up`.
# The Basic value encodes the default local public:secret key pair below.
# Langfuse ingests traces, not Harness metrics.
# A13N_HARNESS_TRACE_LEVEL=verbose
# A13N_HARNESS_METRICS=off
# OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=otlp
# OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=none
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/public/otel
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS="Authorization=Basic bGZfcGtfYWdlbnRfZm91bmRhdGlvbl9sb2NhbDpsZl9za19hZ2VudF9mb3VuZGF0aW9uX2xvY2Fs,x-langfuse-ingestion-version=4"

# make langfuse-up creates the shared local project with the fixed local keys in
# dev/observability/langfuse.py, which the OTEL settings above encode. These
# explicit Host settings do not affect make dev.
